questions.description:
The postfix increment operator yields the old value first and increments afterwards. The snippet below is compiled and run. What is printed?

int x = 5;
System.out.println(x++);

questions.codesnippet:
int a = 5;
int b = a++ + ++a;
System.out.println(a + " " + b);

int x = 5;
int y = x++ * 2 + --x;
System.out.println(y);
